  {
   "title": "Balanced three-phase source",
   "body": "Three sinusoidal voltages with **equal amplitude** and phases **120° apart**. In **positive sequence (abc)** they peak in the order a, b, c: $v_{an}$ leads $v_{bn}$ by 120°, which leads $v_{cn}$ by 120°. Swapping any two lines gives negative sequence (acb), which reverses a three-phase motor. Power engineers use **rms** phasor magnitudes; we do too in this subject.",
   "formula": "\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf V_{an} &= V_Y\\angle 0^\\circ\\\\ \\mathbf V_{bn} &= V_Y\\angle{-120^\\circ}\\\\ \\mathbf V_{cn} &= V_Y\\angle{120^\\circ}\\end{aligned}",
