   "title": "Wye connection",
   "body": "In a wye (Y) the three phases share a star point (n at the source, N at the load). Each phase sees the **line-to-neutral** voltage $V_Y$ and carries the **line current**: $I_{phase} = I_L$. The **line-to-line** voltage is $\\sqrt3$ larger and leads by 30°: $\\mathbf V_{ab} = \\mathbf V_{an} - \\mathbf V_{bn} = \\sqrt3\\,V_Y\\angle 30^\\circ$. In a balanced system the neutral current is zero.",
   "formula": "V_L = \\sqrt3\\,V_Y, \\qquad I_L = I_Y",
