  {
   "title": "Delta connection",
   "body": "In a delta (Δ) each phase impedance sits **between two lines**, so it sees the full line-to-line voltage. Each line current is the difference of two phase currents, e.g. $\\mathbf I_{aA} = \\mathbf I_{AB} - \\mathbf I_{CA} = \\sqrt3\\,\\mathbf I_{AB}\\angle -30^\\circ$. A delta load is equivalent to a wye load with one third of the impedance.",
