  {
   "title": "Why three-phase?",
   "body": "- The total instantaneous power of a balanced load is **constant**, not pulsating (see graph, load angle 30°), so motors and generators run with smooth torque.\n- Three (or four) wires carry the power that would need six wires as three single-phase circuits.\n- Three-phase windings create a **rotating magnetic field**, the basis of induction and synchronous machines.",
   "formula": "p(t) = p_a + p_b + p_c = 3V_YI_L\\cos\\theta",
